# --- registry -------------------------------------------------------------
# Read by setup/lib/models.sh (workloads_all) and setup/lib/budget.py
# (workload_plan). Started only through bench/sideserver.py --workload.
WORKLOAD_TITLE=Chatterbox-Multilingual TTS (torch CPU, media/audio venv) · MIT · voice cloning
WORKLOAD_KIND=audio
WORKLOAD_MODE=batch
# Why this model: the torch-lane quality pick, and the capability pick —
# zero-shot voice cloning from ~5 s of reference audio, 23 languages
# INCLUDING GERMAN, MIT licence (the cleanest in its class; Chatterbox-
# TURBO, the faster sibling, is English-only and therefore not this
# profile). First real tenant of media/audio/ — the border rules of
# media/README.md apply: own venv under @HOME@/.venvs/media-audio, nothing
# imported by the base stack.
#
# CPU torch ON PURPOSE: ROCm torch on gfx1151 is an unmeasured backend —
# an experiment, not a default (media/README.md). The cost of that choice
# is what the first bench measures; a GPU lane would re-measure everything.
#
# --seed 42 pinned for the same reason as qwen3-tts.env: unpinned sampling
# makes two runs two experiments. Determinism is OBSERVED by audiobench
# (distinct_outputs), not assumed — chatterbox samples autoregressively
# and documents no seed contract.
WORKLOAD_CMD=@HOME@/.venvs/media-audio/bin/python \
  @HOME@/.venvs/media-audio/bin/chatterbox-tts-cli --lang de --seed 42
WORKLOAD_PROMPT=Es war einmal ein alter Leuchtturm an einer felsigen Küste, der jede Nacht sein warmes Licht über das dunkle Meer schickte.
# The weights live in the Hugging Face cache under a content-addressed
# path that does not exist before the first run and cannot be named here.
# `hf-cache` is budget.py's CONTRACT KEYWORD for that state (the first
# version was a never-resolving path exploited for its side effect —
# review, 01.09.2026): the guard names the state out loud until the
# measured figures below take over.
WORKLOAD_FILES=hf-cache
# WORKLOAD_SOURCE — where the weights come from, machine-readable
# (URLs, space-separated); fetched 01.09.2026. The prose history
# stays in the comments above; this line is for tooling and for
# the next machine.
WORKLOAD_SOURCE=https://huggingface.co/ResembleAI/chatterbox/tree/5bb1f6ee58e50c3b8d408bc82a6d3740c2db6e18
# WORKLOAD_SMOKE_SHA256 — the DETERMINISM PIN: the exact output hash a
# 1-rep bench at this profile's settings on the pinned build must
# reproduce. tests/live_media.sh verifies it through the fence; a flip
# means build, weights or flags changed the output — the sharpest
# regression instrument this stack has. Re-declare on any deliberate
# change, with the report that measured it.
WORKLOAD_SMOKE_SHA256=3556f26701949eb4377e108c0f872ba1596ddb0968f72dd56d451ff56b3fbed3
WORKLOAD_SMOKE_SHA256_SOURCE=01.09.2026, rep1 sha256 of reports 0530/1024 (identical across the revision-pin rework, CPU torch)
# --- measured fields ------------------------------------------------------
# Born UNMEASURED. Fill both figures or neither, each with date + method,
# plus WORKLOAD_MEASURED_ON — tests/test_workloads.py holds the contract.
#
WORKLOAD_GTT_GIB=0.0
WORKLOAD_GTT_SOURCE=01.09.2026, sideserver workload metering at 1 Hz, production stopped, 3-rep bench — a pure-CPU job pins nothing, and 0.0 is the MEASURED zero, not an omission
WORKLOAD_HOST_RSS_GIB=4.4
WORKLOAD_HOST_RSS_SOURCE=01.09.2026, same run: peak RssAnon summed over the unit cgroup at 1 Hz (torch CPU, model load included)
# WORKLOAD_LOCK — the venv's identity, repo-relative (a profile may not
# carry a repo path; budget.py resolves it from its own tree). The lock
# is the torch lane's LLAMA_BIN: the figures above were measured on the
# venv it describes, and budget.workload_plan degrades them to ESTIMATE
# whenever the lock's sha256 stops matching the stamp in MEASURED_ON —
# so a `setup-venv.sh --relock` cannot leave stale figures guarding
# (ultrareview, 01.09.2026). --relock prints the new hash to re-declare.
WORKLOAD_LOCK=media/audio/requirements.lock
WORKLOAD_MEASURED_ON=gfx1151 machine, 124.9 GiB RAM, torch 2.6.0 CPU in ~/.venvs/media-audio, lock sha256:603e09bf6b87
#
# COST, first bench (bench/reports/2026-09-01_0530_audio_chatterbox/):
# median 23.0 s wall for 6.68 s of German audio — REALTIME FACTOR 0.29 on
# CPU torch (n=3, spread 1.3 %). 7.8x slower per audio-second than
# qwen3-tts on Vulkan; what this profile buys instead is voice CLONING
# (pass --ref your_voice.wav in WORKLOAD_CMD) and the 23-language pool.
# Byte-deterministic at seed 42 on THIS stack: three reps, one sha256
# (3556f267…) — an observation about CPU torch, do not carry it to a GPU
# lane unmeasured. First run also cost one fenced cycle to a float32-WAV
# writer bug — fixed in media/audio/chatterbox_tts.py (PCM_S explicit).
